          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/fk036vh7282#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded low on the figures of the date: the figures could give another date. Pencil, five figures run together, close under the paper edge; small and slanted. First 2, third 8 and fifth 4 are plain. The second is read as 1 against the 1 of the roll number on crop 2, written by the same hand, but a 2 is possible, which would give 22.8.24. The fourth carries the same top loop as that hand's 2. Roll number 2154 stands alone on crop 2; the series 2148, 2154, 2160, 2161 runs through this batch. Crop 3 carries a later English note in ink across the roll, 'good condition' over '1. 12. 198-' with the last figure of the year running off the crop: an archive hand, not a punch date. Crop 4 blank."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       },
       "medium": "pencil"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "scan": "https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/fk036vh7282%2Ffk036vh7282_0001/",
